  "notes": "The only Wu model here in a major key and the only one authored as loose. Two research claims drive it. \"Occasionally hand-played and un-quantised; hat patterns irregular\" gives `quantizeStrength` 0.55 and `velocityVar` 0.26 — the loosest pair anywhere in this batch — plus timing jitter well above the boom-bap parent's and a non-continuous hat block. \"Vocal deliberately sings outside the loop's key, producing quarter-tone clashes as a stylistic feature\" cannot be a quarter tone in a 12-tone engine, so it is authored as the nearest available thing: `halfStepDissonance` 0.22 against a major-key table, which produces the same clash one semitone at a time. The melody *is* ODB's sung line rather than an instrument, so `timbreHint` is `vocal_chant` and the countermelody leans on `octave_echo`. Harmony is I–IV blues vamps with i–iv on the darker cuts, so `blues` and `major_blues` are real entries in the scale table. ⚠ `hihat.fillDensity` is 0.45 rather than lower: the pattern is irregular, not absent, and a model that declares a hat block owes every seed a hat. ⚠ `medium`, and the research marks the bar counts `[LOW-CONF]` specifically — \"verses of irregular length (11, 13, 19 bars)\" is an inference in the source, so `arrangement.sectionBars.verse` is authored as a [12,20] range rather than as those three numbers, and it is the one parameter here to re-verify first.",
